>> title: Crispy Chickpeas
>> category: Fried & Crispy
>> tags: chickpeas, roast, snack, crunch, vegan
>> counters: The Bowl Shop
>> aka: crispy chickpeas, crunchy chickpeas, roasted chickpeas, spiced chickpeas, chickpea crunch, garbanzo crunch
>> pairs-with: tahini-sauce, tabbouleh
>> servings: 6
>> time: 1 hr
>> slack: narrow — they are glass-crisp for about an hour and chewy by morning, and a hot oven only half brings it back

>> step: pat them dry until they squeak
Roll @cooked chickpeas{3%cups}(510 g; drained, from two 15-oz tins) between towels until the loose skins come away, then spread them out and ~dry{20%min}.

>> step: roast 400°F (200°C) 35 min, plain
Toss @&(~1)dried chickpeas{} with @olive oil{2%Tbs}(30 mL) and ~roast{35%min} at 400°F (200°C) on a bare #sheet pan{}, shaking it twice, until they rattle like gravel. Nothing else goes in with them.

>> step: stir the spice while they roast
Stir @smoked paprika{2%tsp}, @ground cumin{1%tsp}, @cayenne{1/4%tsp} and @kosher salt{1%tsp} together while they roast.

>> step: toss hot, off the sheet
Toss @&(~2)roasted chickpeas{} with @&(~1)spice{} straight off the sheet, then leave them uncovered in a single layer to cool.
